WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.868
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:06.501
It is time to play a game
of deception

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:08.400
called "True Confessions."

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:17.767
♪♪

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:20.501
My first opponent tonight
is a Grammy winner,

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:22.501
"New York Times"
best-selling author,

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:25.133
and M.C. of
the legendary Roots crew.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.767
Please welcome
Tariq Trotter!

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:30.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.467
Wow.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:33.734
Wow! You just --

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:35.334
You just floated in there.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.501
-You just floated
right in there.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.801
Welcome.
Tariq and I will be facing off

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:41.534
against an incredibly talented
actress and filmmaker,

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:43.133
who you can see every Sunday

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:46.767
in "True Detective:
Night Country," on HBO and Max.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:49.267
Please welcome Jodie Foster.

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:52.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.901
Hi!
Welcome.

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:56.667
Thank you.
What an entrance you got.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.968
-Thank you.
-What an entrance. Now...

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:00.767
-I know how to do it.
-Yes, you'd know how to do it.

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:02.968
Here's how this works.
In front of each of us

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:05.100
are two envelopes
containing confessions.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.534
One is true, the other is a lie.
Once you read your confession,

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.701
the other two players
get to interrogate you.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.601
Then they have to come
to a unanimous decision.

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:16.334
Is it the truth or a lie?
Tariq, you will go first.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:18.434
-Okay.
-Which envelope should he open?

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:20.100
What do you guys think?
1 or 2?

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.734
[ Audience shouts "2!" ]

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:23.167
-I think that's a unanimous 2.

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.667
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:32.734
-Wow.
-All right, this is good.

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:34.033
-That is -- Is it?

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.734
-Well, it's very possible
that it's --

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:37.033
that it definitely happened.
-It's possible.

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:39.234
-It's -- All right.
-What did you have to eat?

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:41.000
-What did we have to eat?
-What did you have to eat there?

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.100
-Um, I didn't go.
-Right. Did you eat?

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.200
-Yeah.
What'd you have to eat?

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.667
-I don't know,
I didn't go to dinner.

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:47.267
I don't even know
where I wound up that day,

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.167
but I just know
I declined respectfully.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.000
-That's a great question.
Wow.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.634
You just nailed it right there.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.634
-If Oprah had asked me
to dinner,

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.467
I would have known
what I missed.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.501
Yeah, I would say.
-Yeah, I'd say -- Yeah.

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:00.467
So, did Quest have a good time?

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:01.834
-He had an amazing time.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:03.267
-Was it a big party
or a small dinner party?

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:04.767
-It was a small dinner party.
-Like, say, what?

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:05.934
-What'd they have for dessert?

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:07.300
-Uh, they had sweet potato pie.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.367
Patti LaBelle made it,
and she was also in attendance.

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:11.534
Okay, well, that sounds good.
That sounds like...

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:13.901
-Yeah, she made it from scratch
or was it just from her company?

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:16.901
-I think she made it.
It was pre Patti pie wave,

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:19.467
so I think she was still, you
know, making them from scratch.

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:22.567
-Pre Patti pie wave sounds
pretty on the level.

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:23.634
-I don't know.
I feel like --

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.834
I just feel like he's acting.

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:29.067
-I'm not that good an actor.
-I concur.

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:30.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:33.567
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:35.367
-Come on!
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:37.434
Why didn't you go?

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:38.734
-I mean, I'm just
an introvert, man.

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.801
I was -- I regret not going,
but I was like,

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:43.400
"Ah, I don't want to go
hang out with the aunties."

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.934
And I should have,
but I didn't.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:47.934
-But who went from the --
from the Grammys?

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.534
-Amir went.
-I know, but anyone else

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:50.801
that we know?
-No, she didn't invite

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:52.701
the Grammys.
She invited us and Patti LaBelle

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:55.567
just on some, you know,
Philly aunties dinner.

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:57.634
-This is the Grammy that had
the salute to hip hop?

00:02:57.634 --> 00:03:00.100
-No, no, no, this was --
I want to say 2014 or '15.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.167
This was a long time ago.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:02.534
-Oh, interesting.
-Okay.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:05.100
-Yeah. I mean, now --
I mean, I would go

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.434
if she invited me today.
-Yeah, today.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:08.300
-But I'm never getting
another invitation.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:11.267
-Uh, all right.
I think Patti LaBelle

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.868
wasn't making her
sweet-potato pie until recently.

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.234
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:17.667
-I think it became, like,
a business thing recently,

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:20.434
so I'm gonna say --
Because I know about this pie,

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:21.767
and I've had it,
but I feel like it was

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:25.067
